think Read KYRI/RADIANT_STYLE to be Kyri, then REMEMBER, REDS, and the top session-log recommends. The thread: the single-line family is complete (line_pierce closed it, 224 image modules), every living REDS row (80-87) Closed or Released, Standfast genuinely clear. The recent logs named the next crux first as a two-line crossing read.
think Standfast check before new work: living REDS 80, 81, 82, 83, 84, 85, 86, 87 all read Closed or Released; ledger under its 24576 byte bound; no open agent-closable red. Clear to take constructive work.
think Crux-first choice: the whole line family read ONE directed line over a scene of objects. The decisive lift is TWO lines read against each other -- do the finite strokes cross, do the infinite lines cross, are they parallel, and where do they meet. This is the crux because it confronts what one-line reads never did: the relationship between two strokes, and the RATIONAL meeting point (a divide), handled the same clear-the-divide way line_project held its foot.
think The math stays exact: segment-vs-segment crossing is the four-orientation test (two opposite-sign pairs, a collinear endpoint touch by on-segment bbox) -- integer compares, no float. The meeting point A + (t_num/den)*(B-A) is held TIMES den (the direction cross) as an i128 pair; cross_is_lattice tests divisibility, cross_point_doubled returns the lattice point or refuses CrossNotWhole -- the exact mirror of line_project's FootNotWhole.
think Designed two hand-verified scenes. Scene 1 (30x26, seven singletons): a horizontal stroke A->B crosses a vertical C->D at the lattice point (25,21) doubled (scaled 28000/23520/1120); C->F is the vertical stroke stopped short (segments_cross FALSE, lines_cross TRUE, cross_only_infinite TRUE, meeting still (25,21)); G->H is a second horizontal stroke, parallel (directions_parallel TRUE, cross_point refuses Parallel). Scene 2 (14x14, four singletons): two diagonals cross at (31/3, 47/3) doubled (scaled 3968/6016/384, 384 dividing neither), cross_is_lattice FALSE, cross_point_doubled refuses CrossNotWhole. Every reading names its stroke by TAPPING anchor blocks -- no per-object label is read, so labeling order never matters.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run of both selftest and witness, no code reds. The scaled point identity (cross of each direction with point-minus-anchor exactly zero) proven on both scenes; reversal from either end leaves the verdict and meeting point identical; SameGroup/EmptyClick/PointOutOfBounds/Parallel/CrossNotWhole refusals by name; determinism. TAME bans clean, width-check exit 0, living-docs lint GREEN, living-card ASCII GREEN.
obs Orientation products stay whole in i64 (doubled-coordinate differences under twice the canvas extent); the scaled meeting point runs in i128 (coordinate times determinant far under the ceiling), matching line_project's i128 discipline for the rational point.
obs Council rota lap: cycling by lap index past the last lap's item 7 (Mycelium), this lap deep-read item 8 of the 27-doc rota -- the compose-not-braid discipline the whole line family honors, owning only the two-stroke crossing test over click_order/click_collinear/line_pierce.
